cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or benchmark, please cite the following work."
title: "Significance Is Not Attribution: The Quantum Machine Learning Advantages That Survive Correction in Network Intrusion Detection Are Classical"
abstract: >-
  A fair, reproducible, multi-dataset benchmark and quantum-attribution audit of
  quantum machine learning for network intrusion detection. Hybrid variational
  quantum circuits and quantum-kernel SVMs are evaluated against honestly-tuned
  classical baselines across NSL-KDD, UNSW-NB15, CICIDS2017, and NF-ToN-IoT-v2,
  with an equal-budget fairness design, operating-point and calibration metrics,
  statistical significance, a NISQ noise sweep, and an attribution audit that
  decomposes any measured gain into its classical and genuinely-quantum components.
