  notes: "Preprint on arXiv (quant-ph). The revised version (v2) shows that neither quantum result surviving the audit is quantum: the quantum-kernel advantage is an artefact of classical baseline tuning under train-to-test shift (test-set shift controls; induced shift on three datasets, 26 runs; a label-free MMD warning statistic), and the 4-qubit hybrid's low-FPR advantage is reproduced by classical twins of its quantum layer (the trained circuit is an exact 81-term trigonometric polynomial). Both models were run on three IBM Heron processors."
